# Preparing the development review workflow

Document ID: `reiyah.perception-rehearsal.checkpoint.2026-09-10`

Version: `0.1.0`

Lifecycle status: `proposed`

## Question and result

Can the existing Engine evidence and record interfaces be assembled into a clear starting
packet for people to test the workflow? The new preparation tool creates separate discovery
folders, a neutral capture index, a common analyst brief, empty conclusion drafts and explicit
effort accounting. It freshly binds the original comparison and observation package. The
actual development preparation covers the same two previously exposed windows and all 725
captures, including 566 camera images and 159 lidar files. No observations were interpreted.

This is a preparation result. The people, viewing workflow and later assisted-evidence packet
are still required. The real comparison remains unresolved at [-8,8] under unit penalties.
There are still zero human judgments and no demonstrated change in an engineering decision.

## Why this is the next slice

The Engine already checks source population, review custody, actual proposal accounting and
joint reference alternatives. Adding another mathematical layer would not supply the missing
physical observations or show that an engineer can use the workflow. The next useful test is
an observed rehearsal against competent conventional practice with equal information and
permission to use the same mathematics.

The [proposed rehearsal plan](../research/perception-rehearsal/0.1.0/plan.json) makes this test
descriptive and confines it to already exposed development evidence. It preserves negative
results: inability to use the material, unsupported closure, lost alternatives, incorrect
enclosures, extra repair burden and equally useful conventional work at no greater total cost.
The proposed 60-scene physical study, its loss, selection and review rules remain unchanged.

## Interface and information boundary

The [interface](../research/perception-rehearsal/0.1.0/README.md) describes the single command.
It reuses the comparison-binding and observation/discovery validators. It adds no matching
algorithm, physical-reference model, statistical estimator, viewer or study-selection logic.

Each discovery folder contains only a fixed guide, neutral package identity, capture index and
an unassigned discovery draft. The index is a projection of the existing neutral manifest,
including every occurrence and explicit availability. The original sealed package is left
intact and its raw assets are not duplicated. The two draft IDs differ; the supplied evidence,
index and instructions are identical. IDs do not establish distinct human reviewers.

Operator-only files retain source mappings and comparison bindings. They must not be delivered
to discovery reviewers. The later analysis folder includes the same empty conclusion template
for both methods. The conventional analyst can use scripts, matching libraries and the same
paired-loss mathematics. Conclusions must be locked before cross-method discussion, and
unresolved physical disagreement must not be relabeled as an adjudicated error.

The effort sheet distinguishes participant, role, stage, category and shared/Engine/conventional
work. It separates person time from compute elapsed time and memory. It begins with no rows;
missing time is not zero. The operator guide requires shared-plus-method totals and actual
combined effort without double-counting shared work.

`PREPARATION.json` is written last after draft byte and directory-membership checks. It binds
preparation only. Existing output identities, malformed requests, changed sources or guides,
unexpected files and interrupted writes cannot acquire a valid completion record. Directory
separation is an operational information boundary, not proof of filesystem access control,
data anonymity, independence, blinding or exposure order.

## Validation and retained corrections

The [machine checkpoint](../research/perception-rehearsal/0.1.0/checkpoint.json) retains exact
source, test and private-output identities. The repository suite passes 295 tests, including
12 new tests of preparation and information boundaries. All 93 measurement tests also pass.
The two complete private kits are byte-identical: 18 files and 1,381,383 bytes each, including
the preparation receipt. No raw assets are duplicated. The two preparation processes took
13.89 and 11.66 seconds on this host; these are local preparation costs, not a benchmark.

The first targeted run correctly rejected changed input digests, but two test assertions
expected the wrong diagnostic name. The source loader's existing `INPUT_DIGEST_MISMATCH`
contract was confirmed, the assertions corrected and the failing capture retained. No input
check was weakened. The first measurement-suite run also exposed a link to this not-yet-written
checkpoint; the missing document was supplied before final validation.

Internal read-only review identified three useful improvements: explicit later preparation of
full annotations and anonymized predictions; participant and work-scope fields in the effort
sheet; and a clear boundary between verified package bytes and coordinator-established prior
exposure history. All three are included. This review is an internal engineering check, not
independent scientific validation.

## Remaining work and authority

Confirm competent independent reviewers, a conventional analyst and independent adjudication;
verify each person's exposure history and a practical JPEG/PLY viewing workflow. Preserve both
unassisted discoveries before any assisted material is revealed. Prepare one exact later packet
with full annotations and anonymized predictions, private configuration mapping and identical
deliveries. Then observe the work and retain original conclusions, disagreements, corrections
and total effort. Repeated usefulness remains untested.

The preparation tool does not verify that arbitrary supplied windows were previously exposed;
the actual run's private selection binds the earlier development history. No human assignment,
assisted release, study selection, external communication, deployment or physical-control work
is performed. Gate A remains unaccepted. Offline Engine implementation and main integration
retain separate explicit operator authorization. Other owner checkouts and research lanes are
preserved.
